        // F_r[x+pos[l]] - F_l[x+pos[l]].
        // Since pos[r]=pos[l], this equals H_r[x + pos[r]-pos[l]]? simply H_r[x]-H_l[x].
        // So condition is H_r - H_l = H_N.
        // Thus if we hash H_k, answer is count of pairs l<r with pos[l]=pos[r] automatically implied by
        // H_r - H_l = H_N? Not necessarily, but H includes shift by pos[k]; comparing with H_N works.
